artifact :the_conversion_card do
  name "The Conversion Card"
  tags :prediction, :legibility, :computation

  prominence :marginal

  prose <<~PROSE
    A single stiff card, the length of a forearm, held in a wire slot at the left edge of the enamel board at #{ref :tangwang_post, "Tangwang Post"}. #{ref :continuity, "Continuity"}'s cabinet prints it at the close of #{ref :the_paired_month, "the paired month"} and prints no second copy. On it: the register year, the roster the conversion was built on, the read fraction as thirty-one over forty-four, the two corrections, the seventh between them, and a ruled line at the foot for a countersignature.

    The cabinet will not score an entrant against a card the line has not signed, and the post will not put a crew on the round against a card the cabinet has not printed. The card is therefore the only document on the reach carrying both civilizations' account of the same people, and the only one neither of them owns.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :mechanics, heading: "Who Signs And What The Signature Means"
    #{future "Peng Lihua"} keeps the roll and the transport book and puts her hand to the card, and what she signs for is narrow and printed above the line: that the named sheet for the month was written from attendance and hours as the stations recorded them, and that the roster figure beside it is the clinic's own series unaltered. She does not sign for the conversion. #{ref :the_great_root, "The Great Root"}'s line service has never been asked to, and the card carries no space for it.

    A card is void on any change to the roster it names. The board's practice is to draw the card from the slot rather than strike it, because a struck card stays legible and a drawn one is in the drawer, and #{ref :xie_lanting, "Xie Lanting"} has twice found a drawn card back in the slot at the start of a quarter.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :limits, heading: "The Thirteen Blank Lines"
    Thirteen of the forty-four names appear on the card's reverse without figures beside them: three scouts and ten grid-hands, listed so the read fraction can be checked by anybody standing at the board. #{ref :nadya_tsoi, "Nadya Tsoi"} has been one of the three since 2085 and has never asked for the line to be filled.

    Nobody at the post can produce the figure that would fill it. The clinic gives a reading to the person it was taken from, and a scout who stands down outside the #{ref :mycelial_neural_mesh, "mesh"} for a night and a day after a walk has no reading to give.
  PROSE

  log "2026-08-09 — The card is a permit to work: one document, displayed at the site it authorises, signed by a person for the conditions they personally verified, cancelled by physical removal, and void on any change to the conditions it names. Industrial permit systems put the authority in the paper's presence rather than in a record, because a copy is acted on after the original has been withdrawn. That decided the single copy, the wire slot, the narrow countersignature and the drawing rather than striking."
end
